    "lawCode": "Amd §6-166, El L (as proposed in S.5180-A & A.5219)",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7196           Revised 1/13/2020\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to certificates of accept-\nance\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a Chapter Amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2019,\nCh.456.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by replacing the term\n\"nomination\" with the term \"appointment.\"\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe underlying chapter sought to preclude identity theft on Opportunity\nto Ballot Petition (OTBP). This chapter amendment makes a technical\nchange to the underlying bill as it is more accurate to say that indi-\nviduals are appointed to service on committees to receive notices as\nopposed to nominated.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 456 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2019, amending the election law relating to\ncertificates of acceptance, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.5180-A and A.5219, takes effect.\n",
